("v1781", "type", "String")
("v1781", "scalar", "ASSURANCE / CONTRAST Light behind the words. A reading theme changed the text to dark ink while three essays retained dark masthead and footer surfaces. The common reading palette now owns the foreground and background pairs across Christian, Dad, Sourcerer and Author reading pages. Headers, essay titles and footer links are checked against the actual supported opaque browser surface. Normal text needs 4.5:1 contrast; large text needs 3:1. Comparisons use the WCAG sRGB formula without rounding at the threshold. The canonical dark footer keeps its own light text. This successor records the current browser pairs; earlier before-and-after evidence retains its original date and artifact bindings in Git history. Gradients, interaction states, native controls, transparency and arbitrary CSS painting need visual review. This bounded report does not certify accessibility. Evidence and its limits Chromium at four declared CSS reflow widths and increased text spacing. Equivalent widths do not record browser-toolbar zoom. Artistic crops, complex painting, screen-reader use and comprehension require separate review. 30 routes · browser-observed · 462 findings and review obligations. Download the complete measured report · Raw bound observations · Questions image diagnostics · All assurance topics Earlier live evidence, preserved at its original revision ↗ Findings and review obligations")
