("v1918", "item", "v1920")
("v1921", "type", "String")
("v1921", "scalar", "Words make worlds. Worlds teach us what to notice.")
("v1918", "item", "v1921")
("v1922", "type", "String")
("v1922", "scalar", "Writing lets me imagine lives, choices and possibilities beyond my own. I want the worlds I make to invite attention: to people, to consequences, and to things a neat explanation can leave out.")
("v1918", "item", "v1922")
("v1923", "type", "String")
("v1923", "scalar", "A question to practise, not a finished answer.")
("v1918", "item", "v1923")
("v1924", "type", "String")
("v1924", "scalar", "AUTHOR")
("v1918", "item", "v1924")
("v1925", "type", "String")
("v1925", "scalar", "A story is a way of paying attention.")
("v1918", "item", "v1925")
("v1926", "type", "String")
("v1926", "scalar", "An invented world still makes choices about who matters, whose voice is heard, and what a reader is invited to hope for. I want to make those choices with care, while leaving room for surprise, ambiguity and a reader’s own response.")
("v1918", "item", "v1926")
("v1927", "type", "String")
("v1927", "scalar", "Where the question becomes concrete.")
("v1918", "item", "v1927")
("v1928", "type", "String")
("v1928", "scalar", "PEOPLE")
("v1918", "item", "v1928")
("v1929", "type", "String")
("v1929", "scalar", "Who gets to be a person in this story?")
("v1918", "item", "v1929")
("v1930", "type", "String")
("v1930", "scalar", "A character should have room to want, refuse and surprise me. I want to notice when I have reduced someone to a lesson, a convenient obstacle or a reward for somebody else.")
("v1918", "item", "v1930")
("v1917", "value", "v1918")
("v1910", "entry", "v1931")
