("v2328", "item", "v2329")
("v2330", "type", "String")
("v2330", "scalar", "PERMISSION\n\nWho gave this system the right to act?\n\nA request to help is not permission to do everything. I want the scope of an action to remain clear, especially when an agent or automation is doing the work.\n\nExplore permission →")
("v2328", "item", "v2330")
("v2331", "type", "String")
("v2331", "scalar", "UNDERSTANDING\n\nCan someone else see why it did that?\n\nAn explanation needs something solid behind it: an explicit description, a source, a reproducible check. Sourcery brings those descriptions and their execution into a common process algebra.\n\nExplore Sourcery →")
("v2328", "item", "v2331")
("v2332", "type", "String")
("v2332", "scalar", "CHANGE\n\nWhat would convince me this change is safe to accept?\n\nA successful example is a beginning. I need evidence about the behaviour being changed, its limits and the responsibilities that remain with people.\n\nExplore Temple →")
("v2328", "item", "v2332")
("v2333", "type", "String")
("v2333", "scalar", "REPAIR\n\nWhat happens when my software is wrong?\n\nPeople need a way to stop, challenge and revise a system. Repair belongs in the ordinary route through the work, rather than depending on the builder being available.\n\nExplore revision →")
("v2328", "item", "v2333")
("v2334", "type", "String")
