("v2395", "scalar", "← All assurance topics ASSURANCE / INDEPENDENT TOPIC Ready for other languages and locales? An independent saga for locale policy, localisable content, language review and locale journeys. The current assessment covers five homepage entry routes. Levels describe evidence maturity within that scope; every topic keeps its own requirements and open work. Internationalisation Level 1 — Scoped Readiness of the currently English homepage entry routes for localisation. Target audiences, supported locales and fallback policy remain undecided. Scope of internationalisation assessment · supported · level 1 — Authored scope and explicit boundaries. Language and UTF-8 metadata · supported · level 2 — Current generated entry markup; presence checks only. Locale and fallback policy · not-evidenced · level 2 — Choose target audiences, supported locales, defaults and fallback behaviour before claiming readiness. Localisable content evidence · not-evidenced · level 2 — Assess message and content externalisation and supply evidence of locale selection and fallback.")
