("v2436", "key", "text")
("v2437", "type", "String")
("v2437", "scalar", "← All assurance topics ASSURANCE / MATURITY & ROADMAP Maturity that shows its work. Each product has a profile across assurance topics. The level records the evidence available for a stated scope; open obligations remain visible. A catalogue label such as “Live example” or “In progress” describes delivery. It does not establish an assurance level. “Unassessed” records the absence of an assessment, without judging a product’s underlying quality. Evidence levels Unassessed — No scoped assurance assessment is recorded. Scoped — Purpose, coverage and evidence obligations are declared. Mechanically checked — The required automated checks pass within that stated scope. Human reviewed — A dated, attributed review addresses the remaining judgment-dependent obligations. Experienced in use — Relevant people have exercised representative journeys and the findings are recorded. Maintained — Ownership, reassessment and regression evidence support continued assurance.")
("v2436", "value", "v2437")
