("v2554", "key", "text")
("v2555", "type", "String")
("v2555", "scalar", "ASSURANCE / PLAIN-LANGUAGE Can someone else understand what I mean? Clarity deserves its own review track. Automatic prompts help locate difficult passages; a reader’s account of what they understood supplies a different kind of evidence. The opening twelve prose blocks of each page are checked for selected specialist terms, long sentences and vague link labels. These are reasons to look more closely, not automatic judgments about the writing. Ask a reader to explain the page in their own words, identify what the work is for, and describe a next step. Record confusing terms and passages, the method and date, and the exact document reviewed. An empty automatic queue never establishes understanding. Evidence and its limits Opening twelve non-code prose blocks and forty main-content link labels on every generated HTML route. English lexical prompts are review candidates, not claims that prose is bad or misunderstood. Preserve voice and technical precision. Zero prompts never establishes comprehension. Self-referential report pages retain the pre-report document hash; this snapshot is not a comprehension approval. 322 routes · human-review-track · 350 findings and review obligations. Download the complete measured report · Raw bound observations · Questions image diagnostics · All assurance topics Earlier live evidence, preserved at its original revision ↗ Findings and review obligations A sample is shown here; the complete report retains every assessment. Review candidates are not automatic judgments about the page.")
("v2554", "value", "v2555")
