("v2638", "type", "String")
("v2638", "scalar", "ASSURANCE / READING-EXPERIENCE Can you read it, enlarge it, and find your way? Browser observations check text contrast, narrow reading layouts, increased text spacing, and real Tab and Enter journeys. The original twenty reader routes and seven image diagnostics remain in scope; the new series, article and design guide join them. Contrast pairs actual computed text colour with the first supported opaque surface. Images, transparency and complex painting remain review work. Zoom checks use CSS widths equivalent to 200% and 400% zoom from a 1280px viewport. A separate profile applies increased text spacing. These are reflow checks, not a recording of browser-toolbar zoom. Keyboard journeys enter the main content, return home, and follow the declared Questions and atlas-place links. Focus visibility and obstruction are recorded along the way. Evidence and its limits Chromium at four declared CSS reflow widths and increased text spacing. Equivalent widths do not record browser-toolbar zoom. Artistic crops, complex painting, screen-reader use and comprehension require separate review. 30 routes · browser-observed · 531 findings and review obligations. Download the complete measured report · Raw bound observations · Questions image diagnostics · All assurance topics Earlier live evidence, preserved at its original revision ↗ Findings and review obligations")
