("v5323", "key", "text")
("v5324", "type", "String")
("v5324", "scalar", "FINDING THINGS OUT Before you trust the reading, check the ruler. Before trusting a number, check what the tool can measure. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A result in a specified mathematical model Three rulers can agree and still all be stretched. More readings help only when you know how the tools relate to what you are measuring. Move the measuring axis in the drawing. The same difference can be hidden from one direction and visible from another. This is a small example, separate from the larger research model. Move the slider. Watch how turning the measuring line changes the number.    ")
("v5323", "value", "v5324")
