("v5516", "scalar", "USING POWER RESPONSIBLY What changes when time is short? Waiting has different costs when needs are more urgent. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. Results in an invented model; real-world testing is still needed An earlier Worldwright project used an invented computer model to compare responses to a shared problem. In its reported tests, the overall ranking changed when the model’s urgency changed. Open each part of the result. Every tested case still involved tradeoffs. The model has not been shown to predict real communities, so its rankings do not tell us what people should do. Open each part of the computer result. Keep its limits beside its ranking.    ")
