("v5799", "type", "String")
("v5799", "scalar", "FINDING THINGS OUT A record can forget completely. Once a record leaves out a difference, that record may be unable to recover it. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A mathematical limit on what a record can tell us The pairs 1 and 3, or 2 and 2, both add up to 4. If the only record is the sum, you cannot tell which pair it came from. Keep the first number as a second record and you can tell these pairs apart. That uses new information. It does not recover the answer from the sum alone. Try both pairs. Then keep a second record and see what becomes clear.    ")
("v5798", "value", "v5799")
