("v5892", "type", "String")
("v5892", "scalar", "USING POWER RESPONSIBLY Restoration without erasure. Hope for restoration does not require calling suffering good. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. An optional religious interpretation In the source’s Christian reading, God enters human life and shares its cost. Resurrection names a hope that brokenness will not have the final word. This is a statement of faith, not a result from physics. It does not ask you to say that your own losses were necessary or deserved. It offers a question about how hope might shape care, patience and honesty.     ")
