("v6658", "type", "String")
("v6658", "scalar", "FINDING THINGS OUT Back where you started. Something has changed. You can come back to the same place with something facing a different way. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A mathematical result; the physical connection is still open Follow the little arrow around the loop. It returns to its starting place, but points in a different direction. The path has left a change that the final location alone does not describe. Mathematicians call this kind of change after a closed journey holonomy. The next question is practical: could a measuring tool notice the change? The personal path offers a separate association with change in a life. Choose “Go round the loop.” Watch which way the little arrow points when it comes back.    ")
("v6657", "value", "v6658")
