("v6751", "key", "text")
("v6752", "type", "String")
("v6752", "scalar", "FINDING THINGS OUT Zoom out. What disappears? A wider view can keep the total while losing where the parts were. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A map of research questions about costs and limits The small grid has eight filled cells. Group them into larger blocks. The total stays eight, but the view no longer shows the arrangement inside each block. A summary can be useful without preserving every detail. The research asks a harder question: which rules and measurements remain reliable when the scale changes? The grid is an example of information loss, not a proof about physics. Combine the cells into bigger blocks. Look for what stays the same and what disappears.    ")
