("v6944", "type", "String")
("v6944", "scalar", "FINDING THINGS OUT Grow a pattern. Keep count. A precise counting rule can connect patterns without making them the same thing. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. An exact counting relationship with limits Begin with the pair 1, 1. Each press applies the same rule: the first new number is twice the first old number plus the second; the second new number is the sum of the old pair. The research connects this rule to particular tiling patterns through several mathematical steps. The ornament here is decorative. The counter shows the exact small calculation. Apply the rule one step at a time. Watch the two numbers. Reset to begin again.    ")
("v6943", "value", "v6944")
