("v7314", "scalar", "A request to help is not permission to do everything.")
("v7300", "item", "v7314")
("v7315", "type", "String")
("v7315", "scalar", "I want the scope of an action to remain clear, especially when an agent or automation is doing the work.")
("v7300", "item", "v7315")
("v7299", "value", "v7300")
("v7278", "entry", "v7316")
("v7316", "type", "Entry")
("v7316", "key", "links")
("v7317", "type", "Sequence")
("v7318", "type", "String")
("v7318", "scalar", "Follow the questions ↓")
("v7317", "item", "v7318")
("v7319", "type", "String")
("v7319", "scalar", "PERMISSION\n\nWho gave this system the right to act?\n\nA request to help is not permission to do everything. I want the scope of an action to remain clear, especially when an agent or automation is doing the work.\n\nExplore permission →")
("v7317", "item", "v7319")
("v7320", "type", "String")
("v7320", "scalar", "UNDERSTANDING\n\nCan someone else see why it did that?\n\nAn explanation needs something solid behind it: an explicit description, a source, a reproducible check. Sourcery brings those descriptions and their execution into a common process algebra.\n\nExplore Sourcery →")
("v7317", "item", "v7320")
("v7321", "type", "String")
("v7321", "scalar", "CHANGE\n\nWhat would convince me this change is safe to accept?\n\nA successful example is a beginning. I need evidence about the behaviour being changed, its limits and the responsibilities that remain with people.\n\nExplore Temple →")
("v7317", "item", "v7321")
("v7322", "type", "String")
("v7322", "scalar", "REPAIR\n\nWhat happens when my software is wrong?\n\nPeople need a way to stop, challenge and revise a system. Repair belongs in the ordinary route through the work, rather than depending on the builder being available.\n\nExplore revision →")
("v7317", "item", "v7322")
("v7323", "type", "String")
("v7323", "scalar", "Sourcerer →")
("v7317", "item", "v7323")
("v7324", "type", "String")
("v7324", "scalar", "Author →")
("v7317", "item", "v7324")
("v7325", "type", "String")
("v7325", "scalar", "Dad →")
("v7317", "item", "v7325")
("v7326", "type", "String")
("v7326", "scalar", "Christian →")
