("v7649", "entry", "v7654")
("v7654", "type", "Entry")
("v7654", "key", "text")
("v7655", "type", "String")
("v7655", "scalar", "SOURCERY · SOFTWARE CREATION WITH ACCOUNTABLE CHANGE Software that\n\nshows its work. Sourcery creates software from explicit descriptions of meaning, behaviour and permitted change. People and AI propose; declared rules and accountable decisions govern what takes effect. The aim is automation people can understand, question and correct. This microsite illustrates the approach; it is not a general app-building service. The Sorcerer’s Apprentice is the fable below: broomsticks illustrate automation, seals illustrate decisions, and a ledger illustrates a checkable history. Or watch the moving picture book. CHAPTER I The Apprentice Once, in a tall house full of books nobody had time to read, there lived an apprentice with a very modern problem: too much to do, and a spell that promised to do it for them. The spell was short. Broom, fetch the water. Don’t trouble me with the details. The apprentice liked that last part best. The broom stood up, took a bucket in each hand and went to work. It was marvellous. It was hands-off. It was, for about four minutes, the future. MORAL\nA spell you can’t read is a spell you can’t stop. CHAPTER II The Flood")
("v7654", "value", "v7655")
