("v7722", "entry", "v7727")
("v7727", "type", "Entry")
("v7727", "key", "text")
("v7728", "type", "String")
("v7728", "scalar", "THE FILM The Covenant, in forty seconds. A trailer rendered entirely from code: a sky computed pixel by pixel, lights that leave trails, the commandments set in type, and a drone synthesised from sine waves and noise. This edition preserves the original film, its captions and its recorded provenance. 00:00 The distance 00:06 The quiet substitutions 00:12 One sentence of law 00:19 Ten candidate commandments 00:29 Many Temples 00:34 Law you can execute HOW IT WAS MADE Procedural cinematography, in filtergraphs. The original film was made with a separate rendering pipeline. A choreography file set the scenes, lights, sparks and chimes; Python, ffmpeg and headless Chrome produced the picture and sound. This edition retains the rendered files and their manifest.")
("v7727", "value", "v7728")
