("v8359", "entry", "v8364")
("v8364", "type", "Entry")
("v8364", "key", "text")
("v8365", "type", "String")
("v8365", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ UNDERSTANDING PEOPLE The same clearing. A different field of attention. Looking closely at one thing can make its surroundings harder to notice. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A research overview with uncertain connections marked Try the two views of the clearing. One keeps several details visible. The other brings the leaf forward while the rest recedes. This changes the drawing; it does not test your attention. The research separates noticing, choosing, awareness and action because explaining one does not automatically explain the others. Try the broad view and the close view. Notice what each brings forward. ")
("v8364", "value", "v8365")
