("v8527", "type", "String")
("v8527", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ USING POWER RESPONSIBLY A failed attempt can still help. A failed attempt is useful when we can explain exactly what it rules out. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A record of failures with their limits kept clear Did the program break? Did a route fail under certain conditions? Was something proved impossible within a model? Or did the test simply lack enough information? Choose a kind of failure. Each leaves different next steps available. Keeping those limits clear can save another person from repeating the same mistake. Choose a kind of failure. Read what it rules out and what it leaves open. ")
("v8526", "value", "v8527")
