("v8801", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT A larger sky. An unfinished explanation. A big question becomes more useful when we can name what is still missing. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A map of open questions in physics Choose a window into gravity, particles or cosmic history. Each shows a different piece of work needed before the explanation can go further. The sky is an illustration. These are open research questions, not discoveries already made. They can still help someone choose a calculation or observation worth trying. Choose a research question. Read what would still be needed to answer it. ")
