("v8911", "type", "String")
("v8911", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ UNDERSTANDING PEOPLE Truth hurts. So can being wrong. Feeling hurt does not tell us, by itself, which explanation is true. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. An invented scene for reflection A fact can challenge an explanation we care about. So can a mistaken accusation. The discomfort alone cannot tell us which one we are facing. Try separating what happened, what you think it means, and how it feels. Which part could you check with a source or a fresh question? You do not need to share a personal experience with this story.  ")
("v8910", "value", "v8911")
