("v8964", "key", "text")
("v8965", "type", "String")
("v8965", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT A record can forget completely. Once a record leaves out a difference, that record may be unable to recover it. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A mathematical limit on what a record can tell us The pairs 1 and 3, or 2 and 2, both add up to 4. If the only record is the sum, you cannot tell which pair it came from. Keep the first number as a second record and you can tell these pairs apart. That uses new information. It does not recover the answer from the sum alone. Try both pairs. Then keep a second record and see what becomes clear. ")
("v8964", "value", "v8965")
