("v9179", "key", "text")
("v9180", "type", "String")
("v9180", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ USING POWER RESPONSIBLY If you could control everything, should you? Being able to control something does not settle whether you should. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A philosophical and theological argument Kenosis is a Christian word often translated as “self-emptying.” Here it means choosing to use power in ways that give others room to act, rather than taking over their choices. Making room does not mean leaving people unprotected. If one person is taking away another’s freedom, care may require a boundary or an intervention. Ask whose freedom your restraint protects, and whose needs it may overlook. This is a philosophical and theological argument. It is not a scientific rule or an instruction about your own relationships. ")
("v9179", "value", "v9180")
