("v9288", "type", "String")
("v9288", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ UNDERSTANDING PEOPLE What are they trying to do? Before answering, ask what the other person is trying to do. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A proposal developed from one recorded mistake Someone might be asking for a solution, testing an idea, telling you something difficult, or asking to be heard. A polished answer to a different request can still miss the point. Try the conversation. You can choose another reply and see another possible response. It is a fictional example, not a test of your listening skills or a way to read someone’s mind. Choose a reply, then read the possible response. You can try every reply. ")
("v9287", "value", "v9288")
