("v9400", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT A matching number is only a clue. A matching number is a clue. It does not identify the thing you found. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A mathematical comparison of three chosen structures The research compares three mathematical structures. One broad measurement makes them look alike. A more detailed count gives three different answers: 744, 24 and 0. Switch the view to see the counts. They separate these three chosen structures. They do not prove that a physical object contains the structure nicknamed the Monster. Compare the broad view with the detailed count. Which view tells the three structures apart? ")
