("v9457", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT What did the measurement miss? Two different things can look the same through one kind of measurement. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. An overview of the current research Imagine two repeating signals that reach the same height. A measuring tool that keeps only their heights may report the same result, even if the signals rise and fall at different times. Try the two views beside this story. The extra timing reference reveals a difference the first view left out. The drawing explains an idea; it is not a recording from an experiment. Switch between the views. Look for a difference the first view misses. ")
