("v9789", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT Can someone else check the result? Keep enough of the method for someone else to check the result. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A recorded computer experiment A final number is hard to check on its own. The computer experiment also keeps its starting settings, several measurements and the results of comparison runs. A separate checking program repeats the calculations from those saved settings. That checks the computer result. It does not replace a test with real equipment.  ")
