("v9841", "type", "String")
("v9841", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ USING POWER RESPONSIBLY Every map leaves something out. A useful map leaves things out. We should be able to find out what. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A software research programme A map makes some parts of the world easier to see. It also leaves out detail. A model, diagram or summary does the same. Lift the layers of the map. Look for where the information came from, which assumptions it needs and what it cannot establish. A complete plan for an experiment does not prove that the experiment happened. Open each layer to see what the map needs you to know. ")
("v9840", "value", "v9841")
