("v9897", "type", "String")
("v9897", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ USING POWER RESPONSIBLY Leaving room is still a choice. Holding back can give someone room. It can also leave someone exposed. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A philosophical and theological argument The argument asks how power can help other people make real choices. Taking over every decision can remove the freedom we say we want to support. But holding back is not always helpful. If someone is taking away another person’s freedom, protection may be needed. Ask who gains room to act, and who is left carrying the cost.  ")
