("v9950", "scalar", "READING AS AUTHOR As an Author, ask whose point of view is present, what a reader is invited to imagine, and what deserves another draft. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT Back where you started. Something has changed. You can come back to the same place with something facing a different way. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A mathematical result; the physical connection is still open Follow the little arrow around the loop. It returns to its starting place, but points in a different direction. The path has left a change that the final location alone does not describe. Mathematicians call this kind of change after a closed journey holonomy. The next question is practical: could a measuring tool notice the change? The personal path offers a separate association with change in a life. Choose “Go round the loop.” Watch which way the little arrow points when it comes back. ")
