("v10584", "item", "v10585")
("v10586", "type", "String")
("v10586", "scalar", "PEOPLE\n\nWho gets to be a person in this story?\n\nA character should have room to want, refuse and surprise me. I want to notice when I have reduced someone to a lesson, a convenient obstacle or a reward for somebody else.\n\nExplore attention to others →")
("v10584", "item", "v10586")
("v10587", "type", "String")
("v10587", "scalar", "CONSEQUENCES\n\nDoes the world remember what its characters do?\n\nChoices should leave traces. Worldwright explores storytelling in which a world can develop through connected situations and consequences, with its construction open to inspection.\n\nExplore Worldwright →")
("v10584", "item", "v10587")
("v10588", "type", "String")
("v10588", "scalar", "CRAFT\n\nCan the same idea find its right form?\n\nA scene might want to become prose, a drawing, an animation or something a person can explore. Creator Studio is the developing workspace for bringing those forms into conversation.\n\nExplore Creator Studio →")
("v10584", "item", "v10588")
("v10589", "type", "String")
("v10589", "scalar", "HONESTY\n\nWhat am I asking the reader to believe?\n\nI want to distinguish invention from a claim about the real world, and conviction from certainty. Revision is part of taking both the story and the reader seriously.\n\nExplore revision →")
("v10584", "item", "v10589")
("v10590", "type", "String")
