("v10601", "key", "text")
("v10602", "type", "String")
("v10602", "scalar", "THREADS / AUTHOR A world someone else can enter. AARON ALDERMAN / AUTHOR Make room for the reader. What does a story owe the lives it touches? Begin with attention, give imagined possibilities a shape, and leave room for a reader’s own understanding. BEGIN WITH A PERSONAL ESSAY What does a story owe the lives it touches? A story can offer another way of seeing. I want to shape that invitation with care for the people represented and room for the person who reads. FOLLOW A THREAD INTO LIFE Three ways to keep reading. Follow attention toward a first sentence, possibility into an imagined world, and a finished draft back into revision. 01 / ATTENTION & WITNESS")
("v10601", "value", "v10602")
