("v10970", "scalar", "READING AS CHRISTIAN As a Christian, ask how love of God and neighbour meets this question, what power should relinquish, and what hope asks you to practise. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ USING POWER RESPONSIBLY A failed attempt can still help. A failed attempt is useful when we can explain exactly what it rules out. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A record of failures with their limits kept clear Did the program break? Did a route fail under certain conditions? Was something proved impossible within a model? Or did the test simply lack enough information? Choose a kind of failure. Each leaves different next steps available. Keeping those limits clear can save another person from repeating the same mistake. Choose a kind of failure. Read what it rules out and what it leaves open. ")
