("v11299", "type", "String")
("v11299", "scalar", "READING AS CHRISTIAN As a Christian, ask how love of God and neighbour meets this question, what power should relinquish, and what hope asks you to practise. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT Slower can cost more. Improving one part of a result can make another part worse. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A recorded computer experiment In the reported computer experiment, slower movement reduces one kind of error but allows more of the signal to fade away. The best overall return among the four tested settings occurs at an intermediate speed. Choose a setting and compare both numbers. These are saved results from that computer model. They are not measurements from a physical device or a best setting for every device. Choose a setting. A larger number means a slower loop here. Compare how much signal returns with how much is lost. ")
("v11298", "value", "v11299")
