("v11408", "type", "String")
("v11408", "scalar", "READING AS CHRISTIAN As a Christian, ask how love of God and neighbour meets this question, what power should relinquish, and what hope asks you to practise. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT A record can forget completely. Once a record leaves out a difference, that record may be unable to recover it. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A mathematical limit on what a record can tell us The pairs 1 and 3, or 2 and 2, both add up to 4. If the only record is the sum, you cannot tell which pair it came from. Keep the first number as a second record and you can tell these pairs apart. That uses new information. It does not recover the answer from the sum alone. Try both pairs. Then keep a second record and see what becomes clear. ")
("v11407", "value", "v11408")
