("v11955", "type", "String")
("v11955", "scalar", "READING AS CHRISTIAN As a Christian, ask how love of God and neighbour meets this question, what power should relinquish, and what hope asks you to practise. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ USING POWER RESPONSIBLY I can. May I? Should I? “Can I?”, “May I?” and “Should I?” are three different questions. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A philosophical and theological argument Being able to do something is about capability. Having permission is about who can authorize it. Deciding whether to do it also means considering the situation and its consequences. Open the three doors. The example is a message that could change someone’s plans. No message is sent; the doors help you examine the decision. Open each door. Each asks a different question about the same proposed action. ")
("v11954", "value", "v11955")
