("v12064", "key", "text")
("v12065", "type", "String")
("v12065", "scalar", "READING AS CHRISTIAN As a Christian, ask how love of God and neighbour meets this question, what power should relinquish, and what hope asks you to practise. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT What can exist together? Some choices work together. Other combinations break a stated rule. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A framework for asking research questions Start with a simple rule: the two numbers must add up to no more than four. Move the slider to change the limit. The lit pairs show which combinations meet it. The second view shows a small example from the mathematics of positive responses. Its formula is available if you want it. Neither view tells us which possible state will happen, or whether a real device can reach it. Move the slider to change the rule. Lit pairs meet the current rule. You can also try a second mathematical view. ")
("v12064", "value", "v12065")
