("v12176", "type", "String")
("v12176", "scalar", "READING AS CHRISTIAN As a Christian, ask how love of God and neighbour meets this question, what power should relinquish, and what hope asks you to practise. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT Possible. Permitted. Still out of reach. A place can be allowed and still have no available route from here. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A framework for asking research questions All three points in the drawing are allowed. At first, the available steps connect A to B, but not B to C. Add the missing step and C becomes reachable from A. The wider research makes this distinction carefully: being allowed, staying within the rules over time, and being reachable are different requirements. Drawing a desirable destination does not build the bridge. Add the missing step. See which point you can reach from A. ")
