("v12393", "type", "String")
("v12393", "scalar", "READING AS CHRISTIAN As a Christian, ask how love of God and neighbour meets this question, what power should relinquish, and what hope asks you to practise. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT Back where you started. Something has changed. You can come back to the same place with something facing a different way. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A mathematical result; the physical connection is still open Follow the little arrow around the loop. It returns to its starting place, but points in a different direction. The path has left a change that the final location alone does not describe. Mathematicians call this kind of change after a closed journey holonomy. The next question is practical: could a measuring tool notice the change? The personal path offers a separate association with change in a life. Choose “Go round the loop.” Watch which way the little arrow points when it comes back. ")
