("v13031", "type", "Sequence")
("v13032", "type", "String")
("v13032", "scalar", "Explore a situation in The Field →")
("v13031", "item", "v13032")
("v13033", "type", "String")
("v13033", "scalar", "Follow the questions ↓")
("v13031", "item", "v13033")
("v13034", "type", "String")
("v13034", "scalar", "Explore power, service and restraint →")
("v13031", "item", "v13034")
("v13035", "type", "String")
("v13035", "scalar", "01 / POWER & AGENCY\n\nWhere am I helping—and where am I taking over?\n\nHaving the power to act does not settle what I owe the person in front of me. I need to ask whose freedom my help makes possible.\n\nExplore power and agency →")
("v13031", "item", "v13035")
("v13036", "type", "String")
("v13036", "scalar", "02 / ENGINEERING & RESTRAINT\n\nWhat must I refuse, even if I can make it work?\n\nA working system can still ask too much of people. I want my engineering to make its authority, limits and costs visible.\n\nExamine permission and responsibility →")
("v13031", "item", "v13036")
("v13037", "type", "String")
("v13037", "scalar", "03 / PHYSICS & TRUTH\n\nWhat would make me surrender the theory I want to be true?\n\nIf I ask an explanation to earn my trust, I have to leave it somewhere to fail. That includes the explanations I most want to succeed.\n\nEnter the working laboratory →")
("v13031", "item", "v13037")
("v13038", "type", "String")
("v13038", "scalar", "04 / SOURCERY & ACCOUNTABILITY\n\nCan the software I build answer for what it does?\n\nPeople should be able to follow a change, question its reasons and retain a meaningful say in what happens next.\n\nFollow the human question in Sourcery →")
("v13031", "item", "v13038")
("v13039", "type", "String")
("v13039", "scalar", "05 / ATTENTION & CARE\n\nHow do I keep caring when understanding isn’t enough?\n\nI can understand a principle and still miss the person. I want to practise attention, listen to correction and keep finding contact.\n\nBegin with care →")
("v13031", "item", "v13039")
("v13040", "type", "String")
("v13040", "scalar", "06 / HISTORY & REPAIR\n\nHow do I repair harm without rewriting what happened?\n\nAn apology cannot make the past disappear. Repair has to leave room for truth, changed practice and the other person’s boundaries.\n\nFollow the visible seam →")
("v13031", "item", "v13040")
("v13041", "type", "String")
("v13041", "scalar", "Enter the workshop encounter →")
