("v14136", "scalar", "READING AS DAD As Dad, ask what presence would look like here, whose room to grow matters, and what a patient act of repair might require. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT How could we tell the explanations apart? Choose a measurement that could tell competing explanations apart. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A plan for physical tests Two explanations may agree on one reading and disagree on another. A timing reference, a reversed path or a different waiting time can help reveal the difference. Choose a check at the bench. These are proposed ways to test ideas, not measurements being collected here. Better tools can be useful even when the result agrees with existing physics. Choose a comparison to see which difference it could reveal. ")
