("v15290", "key", "text")
("v15291", "type", "String")
("v15291", "scalar", "READING AS DAD As Dad, ask what presence would look like here, whose room to grow matters, and what a patient act of repair might require. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ USING POWER RESPONSIBLY Who decides what matters? A score can change when we change what matters most. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. Results in an invented model; real-world testing is still needed Imagine two plans. In this made-up example, A scores 8 for speed and 2 for thoroughness. B has the opposite scores. Move the slider to change how much speed should count. The options stay the same while their ranking changes. The numbers are invented and describe no people. The example makes one question visible: who chose what the score should value? Move the slider to change what the score values. The options themselves stay the same. ")
("v15290", "value", "v15291")
