("v15454", "scalar", "QUESTIONS / DAD How do I stay\npresent as Dad? Attention. Patience. The next ordinary moment. Being Dad asks something different of me from building a system or explaining an idea. I want to be someone my children can turn to: ready to listen, willing to learn, and responsible for the way I use my authority. A question to practise, not a finished answer. DAD Care has to become something they can experience. Good intentions do not make me present. I have to make time, notice when I am distracted, and listen without deciding too quickly what someone needs. These are commitments I want to practise, not a claim that I have got parenting figured out. Where the question becomes concrete. ATTENTION Am I listening, or already preparing my answer? I want to make room for what my children are actually telling me, including feelings I cannot immediately fix. Sometimes the next good thing is to put the task down and stay.")
("v15453", "value", "v15454")
