("v15537", "entry", "v15542")
("v15542", "type", "Entry")
("v15542", "key", "text")
("v15543", "type", "String")
("v15543", "scalar", "AARON ALDERMAN / DAD / 01 Room to Grow Jesus grew. You have room to grow too. Growing Up in the Way of Jesus · Draft for review Someone asks what you want to do when you leave school. You give an answer. A week later, you are interested in something else. Or you hear people talking about faith as though everyone else has it worked out. You have a question, but you are still trying to find the words for it. There can be a lot of pressure to know who you are going to become. Choose your subjects. Find your people. Make good decisions. Have a plan. Even advice meant kindly can make the future feel like an assignment you should have started earlier. If you want to follow Jesus, you might feel another pressure: surely you should already be more patient, more confident, better at praying, less easily annoyed. Here is something worth pausing over. Jesus grew. IN THIS ARTICLE Jesus had growing to do You can take your questions seriously")
("v15542", "value", "v15543")
