("v16782", "scalar", "READING AS SOURCERER As a Sourcerer, ask what is observed, what permits the action, and what would let another person check or revise it. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT Gone from the picture. Still in the motion. Hiding part of a system does not necessarily stop it affecting the rest. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A mathematical result for specified linked quantities The example has two changing quantities that affect one another. Hide one line: the other line keeps the same path. Hiding the line changed the picture, not the calculation. Now disconnect the link between them. This changes the calculation itself. The example helps explain how an unseen part can leave an effect over time. Some hidden parts leave no detectable effect; the next room explores that limit. First hide a line. Then disconnect the link. Compare what each action changes. ")
