("v17061", "key", "text")
("v17062", "type", "String")
("v17062", "scalar", "READING AS SOURCERER As a Sourcerer, ask what is observed, what permits the action, and what would let another person check or revise it. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT What can exist together? Some choices work together. Other combinations break a stated rule. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A framework for asking research questions Start with a simple rule: the two numbers must add up to no more than four. Move the slider to change the limit. The lit pairs show which combinations meet it. The second view shows a small example from the mathematics of positive responses. Its formula is available if you want it. Neither view tells us which possible state will happen, or whether a real device can reach it. Move the slider to change the rule. Lit pairs meet the current rule. You can also try a second mathematical view. ")
("v17061", "value", "v17062")
