("v17173", "type", "String")
("v17173", "scalar", "READING AS SOURCERER As a Sourcerer, ask what is observed, what permits the action, and what would let another person check or revise it. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ FINDING THINGS OUT Possible. Permitted. Still out of reach. A place can be allowed and still have no available route from here. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A framework for asking research questions All three points in the drawing are allowed. At first, the available steps connect A to B, but not B to C. Add the missing step and C becomes reachable from A. The wider research makes this distinction carefully: being allowed, staying within the rules over time, and being reachable are different requirements. Drawing a desirable destination does not build the bridge. Add the missing step. See which point you can reach from A. ")
