("v17608", "type", "String")
("v17608", "scalar", "READING AS SOURCERER As a Sourcerer, ask what is observed, what permits the action, and what would let another person check or revise it. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ UNDERSTANDING PEOPLE One stone. Many histories. A stone can tell several stories, and each needs a different kind of evidence. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. A proposed approach to material and historical evidence Its minerals can help identify the material. Marks may help us ask how it was worked. Its location and surroundings can help us place it in a history. Try those three views. The drawing is not a measured sample. It introduces a research approach that uses the pyramids to connect materials, making, preservation and historical evidence. Choose a view of the stone. Each asks for a different kind of evidence. ")
