("v17830", "type", "String")
("v17830", "scalar", "READING AS SOURCERER As a Sourcerer, ask what is observed, what permits the action, and what would let another person check or revise it. The underlying reading and source evidence are shared. Open the shared version ↗ USING POWER RESPONSIBLY Who decides what matters? A score can change when we change what matters most. The interactive example has its own motion control. Scroll inside it if you need more room. Results in an invented model; real-world testing is still needed Imagine two plans. In this made-up example, A scores 8 for speed and 2 for thoroughness. B has the opposite scores. Move the slider to change how much speed should count. The options stay the same while their ranking changes. The numbers are invented and describe no people. The example makes one question visible: who chose what the score should value? Move the slider to change what the score values. The options themselves stay the same. ")
("v17829", "value", "v17830")
