("v18176", "key", "route")
("v18177", "type", "String")
("v18177", "scalar", "writing/being-here-as-dad/index.html")
("v18176", "value", "v18177")
("v18175", "entry", "v18178")
("v18178", "type", "Entry")
("v18178", "key", "sourceSha256")
("v18179", "type", "String")
("v18179", "scalar", "842b807372c146e5e6d6500e215e85ade3329a8e1cdacbfc42ebc9549d325ede")
("v18178", "value", "v18179")
("v18175", "entry", "v18180")
("v18180", "type", "Entry")
("v18180", "key", "text")
("v18181", "type", "String")
("v18181", "scalar", "AARON ALDERMAN / DAD Being here is part of the work. On attention, boundaries, play and repair as Dad. A personal essay · A working reflection, open to correction I can be busy doing things for a child and still miss the person asking for my attention. The question I want to keep near is small enough to belong in an ordinary day: am I here with you, or only managing what happens next? Being Dad gives care a particular responsibility. There is power in being the adult: the ability to decide, explain, protect, hurry, refuse. I want that power to help another person grow a life of their own. These are commitments I want to practise, with room to notice where my actions fall short. IN THIS ESSAY Be here before solving it. Let protection make room for growth. Leave some of life unmeasured. Return after getting it wrong. Help a life become its own.")
("v18180", "value", "v18181")
