("v18229", "scalar", "writing/faith-with-open-hands/index.html")
("v18228", "value", "v18229")
("v18227", "entry", "v18230")
("v18230", "type", "Entry")
("v18230", "key", "sourceSha256")
("v18231", "type", "String")
("v18231", "scalar", "5ba9af255eb8575cddae57c750892d9e3428db78842cf2631e3259d7d7ae6b88")
("v18230", "value", "v18231")
("v18227", "entry", "v18232")
("v18232", "type", "Entry")
("v18232", "key", "text")
("v18233", "type", "String")
("v18233", "scalar", "AARON ALDERMAN / FAITH & INTERPRETATION Faith, with open hands. How I read God, Jesus, the Bible and other religions. A personal theological essay · A working reading, open to correction I want a faith that can look closely: at Jesus, at a difficult passage, at another person, and at the harm done in God’s name. I also want room for worship, prayer and hope. Careful interpretation belongs inside that life. The reading behind this corpus begins with a conviction: power should serve life, and Jesus gives that conviction its Christian centre. What follows is an account of that reading. I am responsible for its choices; calling them Christian does not make them the only Christian choices. IN THIS ESSAY What do I mean by God? Why begin with Jesus? How do I read the Bible? How do I understand Christianity? How do I meet other religions?")
("v18232", "value", "v18233")
("v18227", "entry", "v18234")
("v18234", "type", "Entry")
