("v18344", "key", "text")
("v18345", "type", "String")
("v18345", "scalar", "AARON ALDERMAN / SOURCERER Make the magic answerable. On building things people can understand, question and change. A personal essay · A working reflection, open to correction I like the moment an idea becomes something you can use: a description turns into a page, a question becomes an experiment, a small tool removes a difficulty. There is wonder in that transition. I want the wonder to survive a closer look. Sourcerer is the name for this side of my work. It brings curiosity about the world together with the craft of making systems. The question beneath both is what would let another person understand the work well enough to question it, use it responsibly and change it. IN THIS ESSAY Start with the distinction that matters. Make meaning something people can work with. Ask who is allowed to make the change. Let a check say exactly what it established. Design for the moment something goes wrong.")
("v18344", "value", "v18345")
